<title>JAPAN: Japan offers 400 bln yen of 3.5% 20-year bonds.</title>
<headline>Japan offers 400 bln yen of 3.5% 20-year bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance said on Tuesday it was offering 400 billion yen of 3.5 percent 20-year bonds through a price competitive auction.</p>
<p>The auction will close at 0300 GMT and the results will be announced at 0530 GMT.</p>
<p>The issue date will be October 21 and the maturity date will be March 20, 2017</p>
</text>
